From 8f2d6a9311f2c0e1a5e62ebf0e9cb459b65c7001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mishka Custom Build <custom@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:16:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] listener: make disabled eBPF configuration a safe no-op

An eBPF listener whose local and shared roles are both explicitly disabled
must remain present in the profile without attaching any kernel resources.
The generated profile also keeps explicit false ipv6/private-address values;
those are harmless when a role is off. Return an inert listener in this case
and request a normal rebuild when a role is enabled again.

The disabled listener accepts same-disabled updates, owns no resources, and
exposes no listening address. Enabling still passes through the registry's
existing rebuild path so the new data plane is constructed from scratch.
